1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:01,393
Seven feet tall.

2
00:00:01,623 --> 00:00:03,301
A dog's head on a man's body.

3
00:00:03,531 --> 00:00:05,149
A howl like a human scream.

4
00:00:05,379 --> 00:00:06,803
That's the Michigan Dogman.

5
00:00:07,353 --> 00:00:09,534
The legend says lumberjacks first met it

6
00:00:09,544 --> 00:00:13,002
in Wexford County in 1887, and that it

7
00:00:13,012 --> 00:00:15,134
comes back every ten years, in years

8
00:00:15,144 --> 00:00:16,293
ending in 7.

9
00:00:16,943 --> 00:00:17,936
Here's the twist.

10
00:00:18,166 --> 00:00:19,613
The story comes from a song.

11
00:00:20,063 --> 00:00:23,872
On April Fools' Day, 1987, Traverse City

12
00:00:23,882 --> 00:00:27,043
radio station WTCM aired a song called The

13
00:00:27,053 --> 00:00:29,901
Legend, written by disc jockey Steve Cook.

14
00:00:30,131 --> 00:00:31,898
He has said he made it up as a prank.

15
00:00:32,348 --> 00:00:33,460
Then the phones rang.

16
00:00:33,690 --> 00:00:35,813
Listeners called the station to say they

17
00:00:35,823 --> 00:00:36,515
had seen one.

18
00:00:37,065 --> 00:00:39,286
Cook has used the song to raise money for

19
00:00:39,296 --> 00:00:40,403
animal charities.

20
00:00:40,633 --> 00:00:42,990
And the legend says the Dogman returns in

21
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:44,320
years ending in 7.

22
00:00:45,070 --> 00:00:46,905
Next year is 2027.

23
00:00:47,135 --> 00:00:49,178
Comment your town, and it could be next.

